13
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:36,100
(EP02 Part 1: Moo's here)

14
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,660
(Jiuzhaigou, current temperature: 27°C)

15
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:40,520
That press tour must've been exhausting.

16
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:41,920
Meet Mr. Wang Feng.

17
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,240
Bai, those leather pants...

18
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,440
Leather pants and a leather cap.

19
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,640
(Leather cap and pants)
You said it'd be freezing here.

20
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:48,600
No wool hat today?

21
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:50,400
(Last season's style,
this season's style)

22
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,480
Switched to leather?

23
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,200
Those thick leather pants...

24
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:56,360
(Everyone loves them)

25
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:57,720
As if it's not hot enough.

26
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:58,760
Aren't those pants hot?

27
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,120
You said it'd be freezing here.

28
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:00,640
True.

29
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,280
Almost freezing.

30
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:01,960
Nights are cold.

31
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,120
Yeah, pretty chilly.

32
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:06,100
(Private chat)
What did you need me for the other day?

33
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,200
Why'd you call me?

34
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:07,880
I went to Shanghai.

35
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:09,680
Oh, that.

36
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:11,360
I was deep in the mountains.

37
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,120
No signal at all.

38
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:14,240
(Still chatting privately)

39
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,000
What's up?

40
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,160
I'm exhausted.

41
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,400
Filming's been exhausting.

42
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,240
How about you?

43
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:18,800
Not bad.

44
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:21,360
(Everyone stops to chat)

45
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:21,920
What are you doing?

46
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:23,760
Cool hairstyle.

47
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:24,560
Know who you look like?

48
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,840
They said Bai looks like...

49
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:27,400
Wang Feng?

50
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,200
Just because of my leather pants?

51
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,520
It'll be like a sauna in there.

52
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,480
Who's wearing perfume?

53
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,520
It's Mr. Huang.

54
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:42,240
What's that?

55
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:42,720
A dog?

56
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:43,700
(Where's the puppy?)

57
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:44,760
(Cuteness alert)

58
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:45,360
What's that thing?

59
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:45,920
A sheep?

60
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:47,880
A cow!

61
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:51,460
Come here, cow!

62
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:52,560
Come here!

63
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,360
Mama!

64
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:56,200
(Hi)

65
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:56,750
Cow!

66
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,960
It's so pretty.

67
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:04,520
Look at those long lashes.

68
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:07,490
Oh my God!

69
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,400
It's ridiculously cute!

70
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:11,560
So adorabe!

71
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:14,680
Is it even a month old?

72
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:15,000
Four months.

73
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:15,560
Four months?

74
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:18,000
Will it look like that when it's grown?

75
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:19,880
Like what?

76
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:20,560
Oh my gosh!

77
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:21,130
(White yaks are a rare albino variety.)

78
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:21,670
(With snow-white fur
and an ethereal appearance,)

79
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:22,400
(they're fondly known as
the pearls of the grasslands.)

80
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,020
(They originate
from Tianzhu County in Wuwei, Gansu.)

81
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:23,750
(They thrive in cold pastures
above 3,000 meters,)

82
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:24,380
(making them true experts
at surviving on the plateau.)

83
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:26,860
(This is what I look like all grown up)

84
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,680
It's just too cute!

85
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:44,020
(Jiuzhaigou Pipa Association
performing Picking Flowers)

86
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:47,110
(Nanping folk tunes and pipa songs)

87
00:03:47,110 --> 00:03:47,780
(Traditional folk music
from Jiuzhaigou, Sichuan)

88
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:48,570
(Listed as national
intangible cultural heritage in 2008)

89
00:03:48,570 --> 00:03:49,340
(A proud symbol
of Jiuzhaigou's cultural heritage)

90
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:50,090
(Blends Shaanxi-Gansu immigrant
and local traditions)

91
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:50,880
(Features the unique Nanping pipa)

92
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:51,690
(A willow-shaped,
three-stringed instrument)

93
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:52,480
(Accompanied by porcelain plates
and small bells)

94
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,260
(Creating a simple,
elegant, timeless sound)

95
00:03:53,260 --> 00:04:05,880
(Rough meaning of the lyrics)

96
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:09,140
(Totally mesmerized)

97
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,040
Xu Fu, come back!

98
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,520
Nothing beats a seasoned performer!

99
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,620
(Art brings him back to life)
My altitude sickness is gone.

100
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,360
Xu Fu, come back!

101
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,760
I'm a little unsteady.

102
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:25,800
My feet keep stumbling.

103
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:26,760
Uneven ground.

104
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:27,760
Looks like...

105
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:29,280
the movie's doing well.

106
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,080
He's got a whole new energy.

107
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:35,320
Great reviews too!

108
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:54,240
That wonderful performance you just saw

109
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:56,520
was brought to you

110
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:59,120
by heritage artists
from the Jiuzhaigou Pipa Association.

111
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:01,880
They performed
the Nanping classic Picking Flowers.

112
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,440
Thank you!

113
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,600
Speaking of Once Upon
a Time in the Middle East, Teng...

114
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,080
Thanks...

115
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:13,680
Thanks for booking screenings, guys!

116
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,000
I've waited a whole year to say this.

117
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,720
And today's the day.

118
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,720
Tianjin has the best food.

119
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:27,110
(Once Upon a Time in the Middle East)
On Natural High, you said

120
00:05:27,110 --> 00:05:28,120
(Tianjin press tour)
On Natural High, you said

121
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,960
(Footage from the internet)
Tianjin has no good food.

122
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,060
(Season 3, EP03 Part 1)
Tianjin?

123
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:31,960
Does Tianjin have good food?

124
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,040
What?

125
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,360
What did you just say?

126
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,800
I've eaten at every stop.

127
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:41,200
Tianjin has the best food.

128
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:43,140
(It's all coming back now)

129
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:45,320
I've finally got my chance!

130
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,440
A whole year!

131
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:50,120
Never thought your press tour
would take you there, huh?

132
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,880
Tianjin has the best food.

133
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:54,880
Delete it.

134
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:55,720
Already deleted!

135
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,360
It's okay, Teng.

136
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,760
I've got another one right here.

137
00:05:58,760 --> 00:05:59,660
(Come prepared for you)

138
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:02,840
(Your reputation precedes you)

139
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:04,040
Just to remind you anytime!

140
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,600
Tianjin has the best food.

141
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,280
You've really gone this far to stop me?

142
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:09,880
(Hu Xianxu)

143
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:10,840
Hello, everyone!

144
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:11,580
(Chen Rui, PhD in zoology,
Chinese Academy of Sciences)

145
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,400
(Secretary-general of China
Scientific Expedition Association)

146
00:06:12,410 --> 00:06:13,400
(Head of the Shi Tan Ji Scientists Team)

147
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,400
Come on!

148
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:16,560
(I'm back)
It's so cute!

149
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,680
This episode's theme

150
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,800
is all about yaks.

151
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:21,440
First, a question for you.

152
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,520
Ever heard a yak make a sound?

153
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:23,680
Nope.

154
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:27,360
Let's play a few audio clips.

155
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,120
See if you can guess

156
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:30,000
which one's a yak.

157
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:31,080
Okay.

158
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,640
(Audio clip 1)

159
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,280
That's the first one.

160
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:34,640
Second clip.

161
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:37,700
(Audio clip 2)

162
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,040
Isn't that a pig?

163
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:40,160
A pig. I'm picking that one.

164
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:42,280
No, that's Teng snoring at night!

165
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:45,720
Then I'm changing my answer!

166
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,240
Now the third clip!

167
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:50,180
(Audio clip 3)

168
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:51,240
That sounds pretty close.

169
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:53,400
Sounds like a big animal.

170
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:54,960
Fourth clip!

171
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:56,900
(Audio clip 4)

172
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:58,600
Okay!

173
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:01,240
Which of those four was a yak?

174
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,160
The first one!

175
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:03,680
Number four!

176
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,480
I'll go with one.

177
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,240
Number one.

178
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,280
The real yak sound

179
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,280
was number four.

180
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:10,920
The one that sounded like a pig.

181
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,360
That's why yaks

182
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,960
are sometimes called

183
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:17,200
pig-sounding cattle.

184
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,440
They sound like pigs.

185
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:21,640
Yaks are naturally herd animals.

186
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,080
They have

187
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,880
a really effective way to communicate.

188
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:26,960
Up on the plateau,

189
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:29,040
yaks use specific calls

190
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:31,120
and movements to communicate.

191
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,720
One yak sends a signal,

192
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,400
and the whole herd responds.

193
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,040
It's just like when we're chatting.

194
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,560
I start a sentence,

195
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,280
and you finish it.

196
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,960
Your next challenge

197
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:41,720
will test whether

198
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:43,720
you're as in sync as a herd of yaks.

199
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,080
Alright, let's get down!

200
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:45,860
(We're done already?)
Let's go!

201
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:46,640
Let's go!

202
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:48,080
(Happy yak clocking out)
Wow, it's so obedient!

203
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,240
So lively after clocking out.

204
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:54,840
Our next challenge is called

205
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:57,020
Yak Finish-the-Line Challenge.

206
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,400
(Yak Finish-the-Line Challenge)
Two teams compete.

207
00:07:58,400 --> 00:07:59,360
Four players per team.

208
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,760
They'll take turns playing.

209
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:02,400
(Bai Jingting)
Two players act out a scene.

210
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,440
The other two guess.

211
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,880
The actors will be given

212
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:07,320
(Jia Bing)
a common everyday phrase.

213
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,680
(Huang Jingyu)
They'll act out a scene

214
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,880
to get their teammates

215
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:14,040
(Wang Anyu)
to guess the phrase.

216
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:16,360
(Fan Chengcheng)
The other team can buzz in anytime.

217
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:19,240
A successful steal means
no points for the acting team.

218
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,720
Each team gets ten minutes.

219
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:21,800
Pick our own teams?

220
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:26,580
(Goofball and dummy)

221
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,560
We could read each other's minds.

222
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,880
We just locked eyes.

223
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:31,440
Wait, don't we usually
split down the middle?

224
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:33,060
(Then let's..)

225
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:35,280
Then one, three, five, seven.

226
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:40,480
You just wanna put Anyu
and Bai on the same team.

227
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:41,840
Nobody can come between us.

228
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:43,460
(The old guy knows how to make room)

229
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:46,520
Then we'll take one, three, five, seven.

230
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,160
Seriously? One, three, five, seven?

231
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:50,780
(Playing along with their nonsense)
We're really doing that?

232
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:51,960
Fine!

233
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,700
(Giving in)

234
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:53,960
You two go first.

235
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,040
Okay.

236
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,120
The two with the best chemistry.

237
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,680
Come on.

238
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:58,600
Start acting!

239
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:03,620
(Team Bai Jingting, Hu Xianxu,
Wang Anyu, Wang Churan, act, guess)

240
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:06,740
(Clue: "Bie shuo hua, wen wo")
[*Don't talk. Kiss me]

241
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:08,860
(Starting off strong)

242
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:15,100
(Don't talk. Kiss me)

243
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:16,130
Your turn.

244
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,680
(Buzzes in)
Don't talk. Kiss me!

245
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:33,780
(The one who knows
YuTing Clear Skies best)

246
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:38,660
(As hyped as hearing
their number called at a restaurant)

247
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:40,180
(What's all the hype about?)

248
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,160
So all along, we've had...

249
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:45,820
(Welcome to the family)

250
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:49,180
(Clue: "Dao di na cuo le")
[*What exactly did I do wrong?]

251
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:50,450
(What exactly did I do wrong?)

252
00:09:50,450 --> 00:09:51,840
Don't give me

253
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,520
all that nonsense!

254
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,800
I don't wanna hear any excuses!

255
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,760
(Loving this drama)

256
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:58,080
No!

257
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:58,840
Just tell me right now!

258
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,000
Then you've gotta tell me!

259
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:00,800
Tell me...

260
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:03,300
(Tell me "what I did wrong")

261
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:04,200
"Dao di cuo zai na"!
[*Where exactly did I go wrong?]

262
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,000
("Ni gao su wo, dao di cuo zai na")
[*Tell me where I went wrong]

263
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:06,100
(So close)

264
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:07,680
(On the tip of your tongue)

265
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:08,960
"Wo dao di cuo zai na li".
[*Where exactly did I go wrong?]

266
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:10,550
"Wo dao di cuo zai na"?
[*Where did I go wrong?]

267
00:10:10,550 --> 00:10:11,260
("Ni gao su wo, dao di cuo zai na")
[*Tell me where I went wrong]

268
00:10:11,630 --> 00:10:12,780
"Wo dao di cuo na le"!
[*What exactly did I do wrong?]

269
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:13,500
("Ni gao su wo, dao di cuo na le")
[*Tell me what I did wrong]

270
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:15,320
Characters are correct!

271
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,260
(Just rearrange them)

272
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:16,980
